B.YS=new A.j0("\ud83d\udd2c","Le cycle de l'eau dans le Coran","The water cycle in the Quran","Le Coran d\xe9crit le cycle de l'eau avec pr\xe9cision 1400 ans avant la science moderne : \xab N'as-tu pas vu qu'Allah fait descendre du ciel de l'eau, puis Il l'achemine vers des sources dans la terre ? \xbb (Az-Zumar, 39:21). La description coranique inclut l'\xe9vaporation, la condensation et les pr\xe9cipitations.",'The Quran describes the water cycle with precision 1,400 years before modern science: "Have you not seen that Allah sends down water from the sky, then He causes it to travel through the earth as springs?" (Az-Zumar, 39:21). The Quranic description includes evaporation, condensation and precipitation.')
B.YU=new A.j0("\ud83d\udc41\ufe0f","Ibn al-Haytham, p\xe8re de l'optique","Ibn al-Haytham, father of optics","Le savant musulman Ibn al-Haytham (965-1040) est consid\xe9r\xe9 comme le p\xe8re de l'optique moderne. Son \xab Livre de l'optique \xbb a r\xe9volutionn\xe9 la compr\xe9hension de la vision et de la lumi\xe8re. Il a invent\xe9 la camera obscura et pos\xe9 les bases de la m\xe9thode scientifique exp\xe9rimentale, 600 ans avant Galil\xe9e.",'Muslim scholar Ibn al-Haytham (965\u20131040) is considered the father of modern optics. His "Book of Optics" revolutionised the understanding of vision and light. He invented the camera obscura and laid the foundations of the experimental scientific method, 600 years before Galileo.')
B.YV=new A.j0("\ud83c\udfe5","Les premiers h\xf4pitaux","The first hospitals","Les premiers h\xf4pitaux modernes (Bimaristans) ont \xe9t\xe9 fond\xe9s dans le monde musulman d\xe8s le 8e si\xe8cle. L'h\xf4pital Al-Mansur au Caire (1284) avait des d\xe9partements sp\xe9cialis\xe9s, des pharmacies, et soignait gratuitement tous les patients, quelle que soit leur religion ou leur statut social.","The first modern hospitals (Bimaristans) were founded in the Muslim world as early as the 8th century. Al-Mansur Hospital in Cairo (1284) had specialised departments, pharmacies, and treated all patients free of charge, regardless of their religion or social status.")
B.YZ=new A.j0("\ud83c\udf0d","Les montagnes comme des piquets","Mountains as pegs","Le Coran compare les montagnes \xe0 des piquets : \xab N'avons-Nous pas fait de la terre une couche, et des montagnes des piquets ? \xbb (An-Naba, 78:6-7). La g\xe9ologie moderne a confirm\xe9 que les montagnes ont des racines profondes qui stabilisent la cro\xfbte terrestre, exactement comme des piquets.",'The Quran compares mountains to pegs: "Have We not made the earth a resting place, and the mountains as pegs?" (An-Naba, 78:6\u20137). Modern geology has confirmed that mountains have deep roots that stabilise the earth\'s crust, exactly like pegs.')
B.YT=new A.j0("\u2708\ufe0f","Abbas ibn Firnas et le vol","Abbas ibn Firnas and flight","En 875, Abbas ibn Firnas, un inventeur andalou, a r\xe9alis\xe9 le premier vol plan\xe9 de l'histoire en se lan\xe7ant depuis une colline de Cordoue avec des ailes fabriqu\xe9es. Il a plan\xe9 pendant plusieurs minutes avant d'atterrir. C'\xe9tait 600 ans avant L\xe9onard de Vinci et plus de 1000 ans avant les fr\xe8res Wright.","In 875, Abbas ibn Firnas, an Andalusian inventor, achieved the first gliding flight in history by launching himself from a hill in C\xf3rdoba with crafted wings. He glided for several minutes before landing. This was 600 years before Leonardo da Vinci and over 1,000 years before the Wright brothers.")
B.YY=new A.j0("\ud83d\udd22","Al-Khwarizmi et l'alg\xe8bre","Al-Khwarizmi and algebra","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Khwarizmi (780-850) est le p\xe8re de l'alg\xe8bre. Le mot \xab alg\xe8bre \xbb vient du titre de son livre \xab Al-Jabr \xbb. Le mot \xab algorithme \xbb vient de la latinisation de son nom. Ses travaux en math\xe9matiques ont r\xe9volutionn\xe9 la science et sont \xe0 la base de l'informatique moderne.",'Muhammad ibn Musa al-Khwarizmi (780\u2013850) is the father of algebra. The word "algebra" comes from the title of his book "Al-Jabr." The word "algorithm" comes from the Latinisation of his name. His work in mathematics revolutionised science and forms the basis of modern computing.')
B.YW=new A.j0("\ud83e\uddec","L'embryologie dans le Coran","Embryology in the Quran","Le Coran d\xe9crit les \xe9tapes du d\xe9veloppement embryonnaire avec une pr\xe9cision remarquable : nutfa (goutte), alaqa (adh\xe9rence), mudgha (morceau m\xe2ch\xe9), puis os recouverts de chair. Le Professeur Keith Moore, \xe9minent embryologiste, a reconnu que ces descriptions ne pouvaient pas provenir des connaissances humaines du 7e si\xe8cle.","The Quran describes the stages of embryonic development with remarkable precision: nutfa (drop), alaqa (clinging), mudgha (chewed lump), then bones covered with flesh. Professor Keith Moore, a renowned embryologist, acknowledged that these descriptions could not have come from human knowledge of the 7th century.")
B.YX=new A.j0("\ud83d\udcda","La Maison de la Sagesse","The House of Wisdom","La Maison de la Sagesse (Bayt al-Hikma) fond\xe9e \xe0 Bagdad au 9e si\xe8cle \xe9tait la plus grande biblioth\xe8que et centre de traduction au monde. Des savants de toutes religions y traduisaient les \u0153uvres grecques, persanes et indiennes en arabe, pr\xe9servant et enrichissant le savoir antique pour les g\xe9n\xe9rations futures.","The House of Wisdom (Bayt al-Hikma) founded in Baghdad in the 9th century was the largest library and translation centre in the world. Scholars of all religions translated Greek, Persian and Indian works into Arabic, preserving and enriching ancient knowledge for future generations.")
B.YR=new A.j0("\ud83c\udf0a","La barri\xe8re entre les mers","The barrier between seas","Le Coran mentionne une barri\xe8re invisible entre deux mers qui se rencontrent : \xab Il a donn\xe9 libre cours aux deux mers pour se rencontrer ; il y a entre elles une barri\xe8re qu'elles ne d\xe9passent pas. \xbb (Ar-Rahman, 55:19-20). L'oc\xe9anographie moderne a confirm\xe9 l'existence de ces fronti\xe8res de salinit\xe9 entre les masses d'eau.",'The Quran mentions an invisible barrier between two seas that meet: "He released the two seas, meeting side by side; between them is a barrier they do not transgress." (Ar-Rahman, 55:19\u201320). Modern oceanography has confirmed the existence of these salinity boundaries between water masses.')
B.YQ=new A.j0("\ud83d\udd4c","L'Universit\xe9 Al-Qarawiyyin","Al-Qarawiyyin University","Fond\xe9e en 859 par Fatima al-Fihri \xe0 F\xe8s (Maroc), Al-Qarawiyyin est reconnue par l'UNESCO comme la plus ancienne universit\xe9 encore en activit\xe9 au monde. Elle a form\xe9 des \xe9rudits de toutes disciplines pendant plus de 1100 ans et a inspir\xe9 les universit\xe9s europ\xe9ennes m\xe9di\xe9vales.","Founded in 859 by Fatima al-Fihri in Fez (Morocco), Al-Qarawiyyin is recognised by UNESCO as the oldest continuously operating university in the world. It has trained scholars across all disciplines for over 1,100 years and inspired medieval European universities.")
B.a6O=s([B.YS,B.YU,B.YV,B.YZ,B.YT,B.YY,B.YW,B.YX,B.YR,B.YQ],A.al("D<j0>"))
