B.bX=new A.jh(4,"defiJour")
B.UQ=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi du jour","Aujourd'hui, essaie de lire 5 versets du Coran avec leur traduction. Pas de vitesse, juste de la compr\xe9hension. Tu acceptes le d\xe9fi ?","Accepter","quran","Today's challenge","Today, try to read 5 verses of the Quran with their translation. No rush, just understanding. Will you accept the challenge?","Accept")
B.V4=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi du jour","Apprends un nouveau nom d'Allah aujourd'hui. Comprends son sens, m\xe9dite dessus. Il y en a 99, chacun est un tr\xe9sor.","D\xe9couvrir","spiritualite","Today's challenge","Learn a new name of Allah today. Understand its meaning, meditate on it. There are 99, each one is a treasure.","Discover")
B.Vs=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi du jour","Lis un hadith et essaie de l'appliquer aujourd'hui. Juste un seul. La sunna se vit au quotidien, pas seulement dans les livres.","Lire un hadith","hadith","Today's challenge","Read a hadith and try to apply it today. Just one. The Sunnah is lived daily, not just in books.","Read a hadith")
B.V2=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi du jour","Dis \xab Astaghfirullah \xbb 100 fois aujourd'hui. \xc7a prend 3 minutes. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa le faisait plus de 70 fois par jour alors qu'il \xe9tait d\xe9j\xe0 pardonn\xe9.",null,null,"Today's challenge",'Say "Astaghfirullah" 100 times today. Takes 3 minutes. The Prophet \ufdfa did it more than 70 times a day even though he was already forgiven.',null)
B.Uv=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi famille","Raconte une histoire de proph\xe8te \xe0 un enfant de ta famille aujourd'hui. Tu seras r\xe9compens\xe9(e) pour chaque mot de bien que tu transmets.","Histoires","famille","Family challenge","Tell a prophet's story to a child in your family today. You'll be rewarded for every word of good you pass on.","Stories")
B.Ua=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi gentillesse","Fais une bonne action pour quelqu'un sans qu'il le sache. Paye un caf\xe9, laisse passer quelqu'un, offre un compliment sinc\xe8re. La sadaqa secr\xe8te \xe9teint la col\xe8re du Seigneur.",null,null,"Kindness challenge","Do a good deed for someone without them knowing. Buy them coffee, let someone go first, give a sincere compliment. Secret charity extinguishes the Lord's anger.",null)
B.UA=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi m\xe9morisation","Apprends un nouveau verset par c\u0153ur aujourd'hui. Juste un. R\xe9p\xe8te-le 10 fois. Demain, tu t'en souviendras. Dans un an, tu auras appris 365 versets.","M\xe9moriser","quran","Memorization challenge","Memorize a new verse today. Just one. Repeat it 10 times. Tomorrow you'll remember it. In a year, you'll have memorized 365 verses.","Memorize")
B.UP=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi silence","Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit : \xab Que celui qui croit en Allah et au Jour Dernier dise du bien ou se taise. \xbb Aujourd'hui, essaie de ne dire que du bien. Pas de m\xe9disance, pas de plainte.",null,null,"Silence challenge",'The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let them speak good or be silent." Today, try to speak only good. No backbiting, no complaining.',null)
B.Vm=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi gratitude","Ce soir, avant de dormir, \xe9cris 5 choses pour lesquelles tu es reconnaissant(e) envers Allah. La gratitude multiplie les bienfaits. \xab Si vous \xeates reconnaissants, Je vous donnerai davantage. \xbb (14:7)","Journal","learning","Gratitude challenge",'Tonight before sleep, write 5 things you\'re grateful for to Allah. Gratitude multiplies blessings. "If you are grateful, I will give you more." (14:7)',"Journal")
B.V0=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi pardon","Y a-t-il quelqu'un \xe0 qui tu dois pardonner ? Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a pardonn\xe9 aux gens de Quraysh apr\xe8s des ann\xe9es de pers\xe9cution. Si lui a pu, on peut essayer nous aussi.",null,null,"Forgiveness challenge","Is there someone you need to forgive? The Prophet \ufdfa forgave the Quraysh after years of persecution. If he could, so can we.",null)
B.Un=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi sadaqa","Donne quelque chose aujourd'hui. M\xeame 1\u20ac. M\xeame un sourire. M\xeame un bon conseil. \xab La main qui donne est meilleure que celle qui re\xe7oit. \xbb",null,null,"Sadaqa challenge",'Give something today. Even 1 euro. Even a smile. Even good advice. "The hand that gives is better than the one that takes."',null)
B.UE=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi Coran","Lis une page enti\xe8re du Coran aujourd'hui. Chaque lettre = 10 hassanat. Une page = des milliers de r\xe9compenses. Le calcul est vite fait !","Lire une page","quran","Quran challenge","Read one full page of the Quran today. Each letter = 10 hasanah. One page = thousands of rewards. The math is quick!","Read a page")
B.Uh=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi salam","Dis salam \xe0 5 personnes aujourd'hui. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit : \xab R\xe9pandez le salam entre vous. \xbb C'est la mani\xe8re la plus simple de gagner des hassanat et de cr\xe9er du lien.",null,null,"Salam challenge",'Greet 5 people with salam today. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Spread salam among you." It\'s the easiest way to earn hasanah and create connection.',null)
B.Ur=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi tahajjud","Ce soir, essaie de te lever 15 minutes avant le fajr pour prier 2 rak'at. Le tahajjud est la pri\xe8re des \xe9lites. Tu es capable.",null,null,"Tahajjud challenge","Tonight, try to wake up 15 minutes before Fajr to pray 2 rak'at. Tahajjud is the prayer of the elite. You're capable.",null)
B.Vk=new A.aO(B.bX,"\ud83c\udfaf","D\xe9fi du'a","Fais une longue du'a aujourd'hui. Pas juste \xab Allah aide-moi \xbb. Vraiment parler \xe0 Allah de tout : tes r\xeaves, tes peurs, tes espoirs. Il \xe9coute chaque mot.",null,null,"Du'a challenge",'Make a long du\'a today. Not just "Allah help me." Really talk to Allah about everything: your dreams, fears, hopes. He listens to every word.',null)
B.aaM=s([B.UQ,B.V4,B.Vs,B.V2,B.Uv,B.Ua,B.UA,B.UP,B.Vm,B.V0,B.Un,B.UE,B.Uh,B.Ur,B.Vk],t.Vt)
B.aaO=s(["pointerdown","pointermove","pointerleave","pointerup","pointercancel","touchstart","touchend","touchmove","touchcancel","mousedown","mousemove","mouseleave","mouseup","wheel"],t.s)
B.aoH=new A.kb(3,"\ud83c\udf31","Graine plant\xe9e","Seed Planted","Les actions les plus aim\xe9es d'Allah sont les plus r\xe9guli\xe8res, m\xeame si elles sont peu nombreuses.","The most beloved deeds to Allah are the most consistent, even if they are few.")
B.aoL=new A.kb(7,"\ud83c\udf3f","Premi\xe8re semaine","First Week","Quiconque accomplit une bonne action, Allah la lui multiplie par dix.","Whoever does a good deed, Allah multiplies it for them tenfold.")
B.aoI=new A.kb(14,"\ud83c\udf33","Deux semaines","Two Weeks","La patience est lumi\xe8re. \u2014 Muslim","Patience is light. \u2014 Muslim")
B.aoJ=new A.kb(21,"\u2b50","Habitude forg\xe9e","Habit Forged","L'homme le plus aim\xe9 d'Allah est celui qui est le plus utile aux gens.","The person most beloved to Allah is the one most beneficial to others.")
B.aoK=new A.kb(30,"\ud83c\udfc5","Un mois complet","Full Month","Quiconque je\xfbne Ramadan puis le fait suivre de six jours de Shaww\xe2l, c'est comme s'il avait je\xfbn\xe9 toute l'ann\xe9e.","Whoever fasts Ramadan and then six days of Shawwal, it is as if they fasted the whole year.")
B.aoN=new A.kb(40,"\ud83c\udfc6","Quarantaine proph\xe9tique","Prophetic Forty","Quiconque est sinc\xe8re avec Allah pendant 40 jours, les sources de sagesse jaillissent de son c\u0153ur vers sa langue.","Whoever is sincere with Allah for 40 days, the springs of wisdom flow from their heart to their tongue.")
B.aoG=new A.kb(90,"\ud83d\udc51","Trois mois de constance","Three Months Strong","Certes, apr\xe8s la difficult\xe9 vient la facilit\xe9. \u2014 Coran, 94:6","Indeed, with hardship comes ease. \u2014 Quran, 94:5")
B.aoO=new A.kb(180,"\ud83d\udc8e","Six mois de lumi\xe8re","Six Months of Light","Allah ne change pas l'\xe9tat d'un peuple tant qu'ils ne changent pas ce qui est en eux. \u2014 Coran, 13:11","Allah does not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves. \u2014 Quran, 13:11")
B.aoM=new A.kb(365,"\ud83d\udd4b","Une ann\xe9e compl\xe8te","One Year Complete","Le croyant fort est meilleur et plus aim\xe9 d'Allah que le croyant faible. \u2014 Muslim","The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer. \u2014 Muslim")
B.yD=s([B.aoH,B.aoL,B.aoI,B.aoJ,B.aoK,B.aoN,B.aoG,B.aoO,B.aoM],A.al("D<kb>"))
B.a2L=new A.yF("Tu as \xe9crit une lettre \xe0 toi-m\xeame il y a 30 jours. Veux-tu la relire pour voir ton \xe9volution ?","You wrote yourself a letter 30 days ago. Would you like to reread it to see your progress?")
B.a2N=new A.yF("Un message de ton \xab toi du pass\xe9 \xbb t'attend. Prends un moment pour le relire.",'A message from your "past self" awaits you. Take a moment to reread it.')
B.a2M=new A.yF("Il y a un mois, tu t'es \xe9crit une lettre. C'est le moment de d\xe9couvrir ce que tu ressentais.","A month ago, you wrote yourself a letter. It is time to discover what you felt.")
B.aaY=s([B.a2L,B.a2N,B.a2M],A.al("D<yF>"))
B.aiX=new A.hV("Pourquoi dit-on Bismillah avant de manger ?","Why do we say Bismillah before eating?","\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f","Dire Bismillah (Au nom d'Allah) avant de manger est une sunna du Proph\xe8te \ufdfa. Cela permet de b\xe9nir la nourriture, de remercier Allah pour ce bienfait, et d'emp\xeacher Shaytan de partager notre repas. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit : \xab Quand l'un de vous mange, qu'il mentionne le nom d'Allah. S'il oublie de le mentionner au d\xe9but, qu'il dise : Bismillah fi awwalihi wa akhirihi. \xbb",'Saying Bismillah (In the name of Allah) before eating is a Sunnah of the Prophet \ufdfa. It blesses the food, expresses gratitude to Allah for this blessing, and prevents Shaytan from sharing our meal. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "When one of you eats, let him mention the name of Allah. If he forgets to mention it at the beginning, let him say: Bismillah fi awwalihi wa akhirihi."',"Abu Dawud, Tirmidhi")
B.aiY=new A.hV("Quelle est la sagesse du je\xfbne en Islam ?","What is the wisdom of fasting in Islam?","\ud83c\udf19","Le je\xfbne (Siyam) d\xe9veloppe la taqwa (conscience d'Allah), la ma\xeetrise de soi, la patience et l'empathie envers les plus d\xe9munis. Il purifie le corps et l'\xe2me. Allah dit dans le Coran : \xab \xd4 vous qui croyez ! Le je\xfbne vous est prescrit comme il a \xe9t\xe9 prescrit \xe0 ceux qui vous ont pr\xe9c\xe9d\xe9s, afin que vous atteigniez la pi\xe9t\xe9. \xbb Le je\xfbne est aussi un bouclier contre le Feu.",'Fasting (Siyam) develops taqwa (God-consciousness), self-control, patience, and empathy for those in need. It purifies the body and soul. Allah says in the Quran: "O you who believe! Fasting is prescribed for you as it was prescribed for those before you, so that you may attain piety." Fasting is also a shield against the Fire.',"Coran, Al-Baqara 2:183 ; Bukhari")
B.aj0=new A.hV("Pourquoi les musulmans prient-ils vers La Mecque ?","Why do Muslims pray towards Mecca?","\ud83d\udd4b","La Ka'ba \xe0 La Mecque est la premi\xe8re maison construite pour l'adoration d'Allah, b\xe2tie par Ibrahim (Abraham) et son fils Isma\xefl. Prier vers cette direction (Qibla) unifie les musulmans du monde entier dans une m\xeame direction, symbolisant l'unit\xe9 de la Oumma. Initialement, les musulmans priaient vers J\xe9rusalem, puis Allah a ordonn\xe9 le changement de Qibla vers La Mecque.","The Ka'ba in Mecca is the first house built for the worship of Allah, built by Ibrahim (Abraham) and his son Ismail. Praying in this direction (Qibla) unites Muslims worldwide in a single direction, symbolising the unity of the Ummah. Initially Muslims prayed toward Jerusalem, then Allah ordered the change of Qibla to Mecca.","Coran, Al-Baqara 2:144 ; Al-Imran 3:96")
B.aj5=new A.hV("Comment le Coran a-t-il \xe9t\xe9 pr\xe9serv\xe9 ?","How was the Quran preserved?","\ud83d\udcd6","Le Coran a \xe9t\xe9 pr\xe9serv\xe9 par trois moyens simultan\xe9s : la m\xe9morisation par c\u0153ur (des milliers de compagnons l'avaient m\xe9moris\xe9), l'\xe9criture sur des supports divers du vivant du Proph\xe8te \ufdfa, et la compilation officielle sous Abu Bakr puis Othman. Allah a promis sa pr\xe9servation : \xab C'est Nous qui avons fait descendre le Rappel et c'est Nous qui en sommes les gardiens. \xbb Chaque lettre est identique depuis plus de 1400 ans.",'The Quran was preserved through three simultaneous means: memorisation by heart (thousands of companions had memorised it), writing on various surfaces during the Prophet\'s \ufdfa lifetime, and official compilation under Abu Bakr then Uthman. Allah promised its preservation: "Indeed, it is We who sent down the Reminder and indeed, We will be its guardian." Every letter has been identical for over 1,400 years.',"Coran, Al-Hijr 15:9")
B.aj7=new A.hV("Pourquoi les du'a sont-elles si importantes ?","Why are du'as so important?","\ud83e\udd32","La du'a (invocation) est le c\u0153ur de l'adoration. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit : \xab La du'a est l'adoration elle-m\xeame. \xbb C'est un lien direct entre le serviteur et son Seigneur, sans interm\xe9diaire. Allah dit : \xab Invoquez-Moi, Je vous r\xe9pondrai. \xbb Les moments privil\xe9gi\xe9s pour la du'a sont : le dernier tiers de la nuit, entre l'adhan et l'iqama, en prosternation, et le vendredi.",'Du\'a (supplication) is the essence of worship. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Du\'a is worship itself." It is a direct connection between the servant and his Lord, with no intermediary. Allah says: "Call upon Me; I will respond to you." Privileged times for du\'a include: the last third of the night, between the adhan and iqama, in prostration, and on Fridays.',"Coran, Ghafir 40:60 ; Tirmidhi")
B.aj4=new A.hV("Pourquoi l'Islam interdit-il le Riba (int\xe9r\xeat) ?","Why does Islam forbid Riba (interest)?","\ud83d\udcb0","Le Riba (usure/int\xe9r\xeat) est interdit car il cr\xe9e une injustice : l'argent g\xe9n\xe8re de l'argent sans effort ni risque, au d\xe9triment de l'emprunteur. L'Islam promeut le partage des risques et des profits. Allah dit : \xab Allah a rendu licite le commerce et illicite l'int\xe9r\xeat. \xbb L'alternative islamique est le commerce \xe9quitable, le partenariat (Moudaraba, Moucharaka) et le financement participatif.",'Riba (usury/interest) is forbidden because it creates injustice: money generates money without effort or risk, at the expense of the borrower. Islam promotes risk and profit sharing. Allah says: "Allah has made trade lawful and forbidden interest." The Islamic alternative is fair trade, partnership (Mudaraba, Musharaka) and participatory financing.',"Coran, Al-Baqara 2:275")
B.aj_=new A.hV("Quelle place les parents ont-ils en Islam ?","What place do parents hold in Islam?","\ud83d\udc68\u200d\ud83d\udc69\u200d\ud83d\udc67","Les parents occupent la plus haute place apr\xe8s Allah et Son Messager. Allah ordonne la bienfaisance envers eux juste apr\xe8s l'ordre de L'adorer Lui seul. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit : \xab Le Paradis est sous les pieds des m\xe8res. \xbb Et quand on lui demanda qui m\xe9rite le plus la bonne compagnie, il r\xe9pondit trois fois : \xab Ta m\xe8re \xbb, puis \xab Ton p\xe8re. \xbb M\xeame non-musulmans, les parents m\xe9ritent respect et bont\xe9.",'Parents hold the highest place after Allah and His Messenger. Allah commands kindness to them immediately after the command to worship Him alone. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Paradise lies under the feet of mothers." When asked who most deserves good companionship, he replied three times: "Your mother," then "Your father." Even if non-Muslim, parents deserve respect and kindness.',"Coran, Al-Isra 17:23-24 ; Nasa'i")
B.aj3=new A.hV("Qu'est-ce que la Laylat al-Qadr ?","What is Laylat al-Qadr?","\ud83c\udf1f","La Nuit du Destin (Laylat al-Qadr) est la nuit durant laquelle le Coran a \xe9t\xe9 r\xe9v\xe9l\xe9. Elle est meilleure que mille mois (soit plus de 83 ans d'adoration). Elle se trouve dans les dix derni\xe8res nuits de Ramadan, probablement les nuits impaires (21, 23, 25, 27, 29). Les anges et l'Esprit (Jibril) y descendent. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa intensifiait ses adorations durant ces nuits.","The Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) is the night on which the Quran was revealed. It is better than a thousand months (equivalent to over 83 years of worship). It falls within the last ten nights of Ramadan, most likely the odd nights (21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th, 29th). Angels and the Spirit (Jibril) descend on it. The Prophet \ufdfa intensified his worship during these nights.","Coran, Al-Qadr 97:1-5")
B.aj6=new A.hV("Comment l'Islam voit-il la justice sociale ?","How does Islam view social justice?","\u2696\ufe0f","La justice ('Adl) est un pilier fondamental de l'Islam. Allah ordonne la justice m\xeame envers ceux qu'on n'aime pas : \xab Soyez justes, car la justice est plus proche de la pi\xe9t\xe9. \xbb La Zakat redistribue la richesse, le Waqf finance les biens publics, et le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a interdit toute discrimination. Son dernier sermon rappelle : \xab Aucun Arabe n'est sup\xe9rieur \xe0 un non-Arabe, sauf par la pi\xe9t\xe9. \xbb",'Justice (\'Adl) is a fundamental pillar of Islam. Allah commands justice even toward those one dislikes: "Be just, for justice is closer to piety." Zakat redistributes wealth, Waqf finances public goods, and the Prophet \ufdfa forbade all discrimination. His farewell sermon states: "No Arab is superior to a non-Arab except in piety."',"Coran, Al-Ma'ida 5:8 ; Sermon d'adieu")
B.aj2=new A.hV("Qu'est-ce que le Tawakkul ?","What is Tawakkul?","\ud83d\udd4a\ufe0f","Le Tawakkul est la confiance totale en Allah apr\xe8s avoir fait les efforts n\xe9cessaires. Ce n'est pas la passivit\xe9, mais l'action accompagn\xe9e de la certitude qu'Allah est le meilleur des planificateurs. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit \xe0 l'homme qui ne voulait pas attacher son chameau : \xab Attache-le, puis place ta confiance en Allah. \xbb Le vrai Tawakkul combine l'effort humain et la foi en la sagesse divine.",'Tawakkul is total trust in Allah after having made the necessary efforts. It is not passivity, but action combined with the certainty that Allah is the best of planners. The Prophet \ufdfa said to the man who did not want to tie his camel: "Tie it, then place your trust in Allah." True Tawakkul combines human effort and faith in divine wisdom.',"Tirmidhi ; Coran, At-Talaq 65:3")
B.aj1=new A.hV("Pourquoi l'Islam encourage-t-il la science ?","Why does Islam encourage science?","\ud83e\udde0","Le premier mot r\xe9v\xe9l\xe9 du Coran est \xab Iqra \xbb (Lis !). L'Islam consid\xe8re la recherche du savoir comme une obligation. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa a dit : \xab La recherche du savoir est une obligation pour chaque musulman. \xbb Le Coran invite constamment \xe0 observer, r\xe9fl\xe9chir et m\xe9diter sur la cr\xe9ation. C'est pourquoi la civilisation islamique a \xe9t\xe9 pionni\xe8re en m\xe9decine, astronomie, math\xe9matiques et chimie.",'The first word revealed in the Quran is "Iqra" (Read!). Islam considers the pursuit of knowledge an obligation. The Prophet \ufdfa said: "Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim." The Quran constantly invites us to observe, reflect and contemplate creation. This is why Islamic civilisation was a pioneer in medicine, astronomy, mathematics and chemistry.',"Coran, Al-Alaq 96:1 ; Ibn Majah")
B.aiZ=new A.hV("Qu'est-ce que l'Ihsan ?","What is Ihsan?","\ud83d\udc8e","L'Ihsan est le plus haut degr\xe9 de la foi. Le Proph\xe8te \ufdfa l'a d\xe9fini : \xab C'est que tu adores Allah comme si tu Le voyais, car si tu ne Le vois pas, Lui te voit. \xbb C'est la qu\xeate de l'excellence dans chaque acte d'adoration et dans le comportement envers les gens. L'Islam repose sur trois niveaux : l'Islam (les actes), l'Iman (la foi), et l'Ihsan (l'excellence spirituelle).",'Ihsan is the highest level of faith. The Prophet \ufdfa defined it: "It is to worship Allah as though you see Him, for even if you do not see Him, He sees you." It is the pursuit of excellence in every act of worship and in behaviour toward people. Islam rests on three levels: Islam (acts), Iman (faith), and Ihsan (spiritual excellence).',"Hadith de Jibril \u2014 Muslim")
